OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-$-%%%-!-%%%" ,%-$ -$%%-% ,,
OL,3,GNEWSAParks left unlocked after
OL,4,Abehaviour fears quashed
OL,5,
OL,6,FParks across a Surrey borough will
OL,7,Fcontinue to be left unlocked overnight
OL,8,Fafter the move reduced security costs
OL,9,Fby up to #45,000 "without a measurable
OL,10,Fincrease in anti-social behaviour".
OL,12,FRunnymede Borough Council agreed to
OL,13,Fkeep 24-hour access to Victory Park,
OL,14,FAbbeyfields, The Orchard and
OL,15,FHeathervale Recreation Ground following
OL,16,Fthe trial.
OL,18,FSurrey Police backed the decision, with
OL,19,FBorough Commander Ian Nash writing to
OL,20,Fthe committee that there had been
OL,21,F"minimal incidents reported around some
OL,22,Fof our parks during the trial period".
OL,23,APub: 19-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
